#' hydro_cf
#'
#' @description
#' This data provides a state-level annual capacity factor of hydro power
#'
#' @format
#' A data frame with `49` rows and `3` variables:
#'
#' @source
#' Hall et al., 2003. Table 8, exported as GODEEP/Assumptions/hydro_CF_USA.csv
#' state level monthly capacity factor
#'
#' @examples
#' data(hydro_cf)
"hydro_cf"


#' rooftop_hist_gen
#'
#' @description
#' State-level historic rooftop (small-scale) solar PV generation for 2024,
#' in EJ. Used by GCAM_EJ() to correct rooftop PV's first modeled-period
#' additions: GCAM has no rooftop PV data before the model's first future
#' year, so without this correction the entire pre-existing historic
#' rooftop fleet is counted as newly built capacity in that period.
#'
#' @format
#' A data frame with `51` rows (50 states + DC) and `4` variables:
#' `region`, `value` (EJ), `fuel`, `year`.
#'
#' @source
#' EIA small-scale (distributed) solar PV monthly generation, summed to
#' annual 2024 totals per state; see inst/extdata/rooftop_hist_gen_2024.csv
#' (originally "thousand megawatthours", i.e. GWh, converted to EJ via
#' CONV_GWH_EJ).
#'
#' @examples
#' data(rooftop_hist_gen)
"rooftop_hist_gen"


